text:
I checked both possible problems against the code; both are real.

**C1: confirmed, blocking.** In `src/sales.ts:13` the loop runs while `i <= sales.length`, so its last pass has `i === sales.length`. At that point `sales[i]` is `undefined`, and `sales[i].cents` on line 14 throws a TypeError. That happens on every non-empty input. `summary` in `src/report.ts:4` calls `dailyChanges` with no guard, so `summary` now throws on all real data. Only an empty array gets through, because the loop body never runs. The fix is `i < sales.length`.

**C2: confirmed, consider.** The repository holds only `src/report.ts` and `src/sales.ts`, and this change adds no tests. A test with two sales would have caught C1. REVIEW.md has no rule requiring tests, so I rate this a suggestion rather than a merge blocker; the real defect is already covered by C1.

